      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Letting the wreckage settle\" means stopping the frantic effort to rebuild something that is fundamentally doomed and simply allowing yourself to stop. It is the quiet acceptance that your energy is better spent on the one thing you can truly control: your own survival, rather than a collapsing structure. You don't have to fix the decay; you just have to stop trying to hold it together long enough to find a way out of this cycle.",
      "source": "target",
